# Cursor / AI Assistant Rules — Walsh · Maloy · Dugan Family Archive

You are working on a **static** React + Vite + TypeScript genealogy site.
The full archive ships as a single `client/src/data.json` baked into the
bundle. There is no backend, no database, no runtime API.

Read `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root for the full project guide before making
any non-trivial change. This file is a fast checklist of the rules that
most often get violated.

## Hard rules — never break these

1. **Never use `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `indexedDB`, or cookies.**
   The site runs inside a sandboxed iframe in production where these APIs
   are blocked and will crash the page. Use React state or context for
   transient data. Persistent data lives in `client/src/data.json` only.

2. **Hash routing only.** Routing uses `wouter` with `useHashLocation`.
   Routes are `/#/`, `/#/people`, `/#/person/:id`, `/#/tree`, `/#/gaps`,
   `/#/export`, `/#/changes`. Do NOT use BrowserRouter or path-based
   routing — the site is served from static hosts where path routing 404s.

3. **`text-xl` is the maximum heading size.** Never use `text-2xl` or
   above anywhere in this app. The aesthetic is restrained and editorial.

4. **Preserve the `t0:` / `t1:` ID namespacing on every person/family ID.**
   These prefixes distinguish the two source GEDCOMs (Walsh+Maloy+Dugan
   vs Cranwell) and link relatives across them.

5. **AI features are trusted-family-only.** The OpenAI API key lives in
   session memory only (never persisted) and is gated behind the editor
   passphrase.

6. **Editor passphrase plaintext is `2846`.** The SHA-256 hash lives in
   `client/src/components/EditContext.tsx` as `EDIT_PASSPHRASE_HASH`. To
   rotate, recompute with:
   ```bash
   python3 -c "import hashlib; print(hashlib.sha256(b'NEW').hexdigest())"
   ```

7. **No emoji in UI copy unless explicitly requested.**

8. **Never say "scrape" or "scraping"** — say "collect", "gather", "read",
   or "fetch".

## Project layout

```
client/src/
  App.tsx                 ← Router providers + route table
  data.json               ← THE source of truth (~324 individuals, ~113 families)
  lib/
    family.ts             ← typed dataset loader; exports `people`, `families`, `stats`, `getPerson`, etc.
    gedcomExport.ts       ← client-side GEDCOM 5.5.1 builder
    openai.ts             ← Responses API + web_search wrapper
    researchLinks.ts      ← Ancestry/FamilySearch URL helpers
  pages/
    Home.tsx              ← hero, stats, heraldry, on-this-day, charts
    PeopleList.tsx        ← searchable index
    PersonDetail.tsx      ← profile + Find Missing Info AI button
    TreeView.tsx          ← interactive node graph
    Gaps.tsx              ← research-gap dashboard
    Export.tsx            ← GEDCOM / CSV export
    Changes.tsx           ← edit diff review
  components/
    AppShell.tsx          ← header/footer/nav
    AIChat.tsx            ← floating chat drawer (Markdown rendered)
    AIContext.tsx         ← session-only key + findings + chat history
    EditContext.tsx       ← passphrase + edit state
    WebFindingsCard.tsx   ← shared AI findings UI
    FindMissingInfo.tsx   ← per-profile research button
    ScrollToTop.tsx       ← resets window scroll on every route change
```

## Common tasks

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Install | `npm install` |
| Dev (Vite hot reload) | `npm run dev` → http://localhost:5173 |
| Production build | `rm -rf dist/public && npm run build` |
| Preview built site | `npx serve dist/public` |
| Type-check only | `npx tsc --noEmit` |
| Regenerate GEDCOM | `python3 export_gedcom.py` |
| Apply affiliation patch | edit + run `python3 patch_affiliations.py` |
| Apply military patch | edit + run `python3 patch_military.py` |

Force a clean build (delete `dist/public` first) when **small SVGs (<4 KB)
change** — Vite inlines them as data-URIs and incremental builds skip
re-inlining sometimes.

## Mirroring to the JG3 fork

This repo (Walsh · Maloy · Dugan) has a sibling fork at `../family-tree-jgwalsh`
called **Walsh · Cranwell**. Differences are intentional and minimal:

- AppShell.tsx title says "Walsh · Cranwell" (not "Walsh · Maloy · Dugan")
- GEDCOM filename uses `walsh_cranwell_archive_*` (not `walsh_maloy_dugan_archive_*`)
- Everything else (components, libs, pages, design) should match.

When you make a change here, **mirror it to the fork** unless told otherwise.

## Design system quick reference

- **Type:** Serif display (`font-serif`) for proper-noun headings + body
  sans. Max heading `text-xl`. Body `text-sm` / `text-base`.
- **Color:** HSL CSS variables in `client/src/index.css`. Light + dark
  themes via `.dark` class on `<html>`. Use semantic tokens
  (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`,
  `border-border`) — not raw color names.
- **Spacing:** 4 / 6 / 8 / 12 rhythm. Generous whitespace.
- **Components:** shadcn/ui under `@/components/ui/*`. Icons from
  `lucide-react`.

## Useful imports

```ts
import { people, stats, getPerson, fullDisplayName, parseYear, lifespan } from "@/lib/family";
import { Link, useLocation } from "wouter";
import { useAI } from "@/components/AIContext";
import { useEdit } from "@/components/EditContext";
```
